A short story: In Stranglethorn Vale, Pip the Gnome Warlock coaxed his Succubus, Lilith, through mist-choked alleys. She shimmered, darting ahead to sniff out smugglers, then vanished into shadows to tease a guard before reappearing with a stolen ledger. Pip laughed, muttering that her charm was less a nuisance than a tool—she could charm, distract, and nudge people toward the right path without a fight.

Answer: Succubi are strong at charm/intimidation-adjacent social play, so they help with quests and social encounters even if Voidwalkers look more menacing. [end of text]


